This file states the steps to follow to run this pipeline successfully

Jenkins-Maven Integration:
First install the maven plugin 
Then use any option below:
Option 1: Configure via Jenkins UI (Recommended)
Go to Manage Jenkins → Tools
Scroll to Maven installations
Click Add Maven
Set:
Name: maven-3.9.12
Check Install automatically
Select version 3.9.12
Click Save
This is what the tools { maven 'maven-3.9.12' } block in your Jenkinsfile expects.

Option 2: Install Maven manually inside the container or server:
# Enter the container
docker exec -it jenkins /bin/bash

# Install Maven 3.9.12
cd /opt
curl -O https://dlcdn.apache.org/maven/maven-3/3.9.12/binaries/apache-maven-3.9.12-bin.tar.gz
tar -xzf apache-maven-3.9.12-bin.tar.gz
ln -s apache-maven-3.9.12 maven

# Add to PATH
echo 'export PATH=/opt/maven/bin:$PATH' >> /etc/profile
source /etc/profile

# Verify
mvn --version

⚠️ Important: Even after manual installation, you still need to register it in Jenkins:

Manage Jenkins → Tools → Maven installations → Add Maven

Name: maven-3.9.12
MAVEN_HOME: /opt/maven
Uncheck "Install automatically"

N/B : option 1 above is better

Jenkins-Sonarqube Integration:

Create a token in Sonarqube
In the pom.xml file, edit the following:
sonar.host.url:
sonar.login: input token here

Then: go to Jenkins GUI
Manage Jenkins → System → SonarQube servers
  Name: SonarQube          ← must match withSonarQubeEnv('SonarQube')
  Server URL: http://<sonarqube-ip>:9000
  Token: <your-token>

  For Jenkins-Nexus Integration:
  Create two repositories, go to nexus and click on settings, then click on repositories, after creating 
  Release and Snapshots repos, input in the pom.xml file at line 89, 94
  Then open the jenkins server and edit the settings.xml file
  or in this architecture, jenkins is running as a docker container, so use the following steps: 

  docker exec -it jenkins /bin/bash
mkdir -p /var/jenkins_home/.m2
cat > /var/jenkins_home/.m2/settings.xml << 'EOF'
<settings>
  <servers>
    <server>
      <id>online-release</id>
      <username>admin</username>
      <password>Cadrecontractuel@12</password>
    </server>
    <server>
      <id>online-snapshots</id>
      <username>admin</username>
      <password>Cadrecontractuel@12</password>
    </server>
  </servers>
</settings>
EOF


